{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "בדפקה", :translit "b'dophkah", :gloss "in Dophkah"} {:he "דפק", :translit "dophak", :gloss "knocked"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Place-name בדפקה read as containing the root דפק, 'to knock or beat' (as a heart does)."}], :frame {:text "The desert station-name Dophkah (Numbers 33:12) is traditionally linked by folk etymology to the root דפק, meaning 'to knock or beat.' The Israelites' hearts knocked with anxiety because they lacked bread; the place was later named for this episode (cf. Exodus 16:1–3 where the congregation complains of hunger at the start of the manna narrative).", :sources ["Numbers 33:12" "Exodus 16:1–3"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Place-name בדפקה read as containing the root דפק, 'to knock or beat' (as a heart does).", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:32:40.193841854Z", :model "glm-5.2"}